# The DDF sources go into the built zip byte for byte
# (tools/generate-ddf-header.js), and that build is only deterministic if a
# clone reproduces those bytes exactly. Some of these .bdf files contain
# CRLF and some LF - mixed, in the same directory - so any translation
# changes half of them: the same source would build a different DDF on a
# Linux checkout, --check would report stale on a clean tree, and the fonts
# compiled into the firmware would differ from the ones the designer
# renders with.
ddf-source*/** -text

# The generated DDF headers are written with LF by tools/pre_build_ddf.py,
# which compares bytes before rewriting. Checked out with CRLF (Git for
# Windows' core.autocrlf=true, the default on the PC the environment moved to
# on 2026-09-27) every build rewrote them, the tree was never clean - which a
# release needs - and the DDF freshness check called two of them stale.
src/boards/*/ddf_zip.h text eol=lf

# A byte-for-byte copy of schaltli-designer's lib/placeholders/vectors.json,
# compared byte for byte by test/test_placeholders - both are kept LF, or
# core.autocrlf would make the copy differ on one checkout and not the other.
test/test_placeholders/placeholder-vectors.json text eol=lf
